descriptions:
An in-depth political economy analysis of the nine states within the Legal Amazon of Brazil, identifying the opportunities and barriers to interventions designed to tackle deforestation; 
Paying for nature in Brazil: An evaluation of barriers and opportunities to incentivise the protection of standing forests through payment for ecosystem services;  
Donor activities and Programme/Partnership Opportunities: A report which outlines key donor activities and partnership opportunities in Brazil, in supporting approaches to shift incentives in the AFOLU sectors and support for further research by independent science and civil society organisations.

The project will establish an independent secretariat and expert support function to enhance functionality of the Diplomatic Contact Group and drive effective diplomatic action for humanitarian access by providing critical technical and operational capacity to:
- help identify access barriers and provide recommendations for Diplomatic Contact Group members to exert diplomatic efforts in the pursuit of enhanced humanitarian access and protection to conflict affected populations; 
- analyse and help to mitigate security risks to aid workers, building on United Nations Security Council Resolution 2730
- create a mechanism that enables other Diplomatic Contact Group members to contribute financial assistance to the project to support its sustainability in the longer-term;
- provide an independent secretariat to ensure the effective functioning of the Diplomatic Contact Group.
